// The largest value an index takes over the loop, as C text in 64 bits, and
// the clauses that make it so. A literal is itself; a name the body leaves
// alone, a counter at entry and a second counter must not be negative (a
// clause each); a counter reaches its limit less one (its limit must exist, a
// clause when it is len(xs)); a second counter reaches its entry value plus,
// for each counter of the condition, the room between the counter and its
// limit less one; a local is its definition's terms.

lx_hi(int lg_e, int lg_id, int lg_lo, int lg_hi, int lg_dp) {
